y plausible benefit, not a declaration that the quoted claim is demonstrated. Given crowded journeys, I favour immediate coverage over staging, while acknowledging uncertain benefits and burdens.\n\n### 3. Decisive reasons\nRandomised allocation, identical testing and complete follow-up support the observed reduction among enrolled passengers: 40/2,000 versus 80/2,000 infections; RR 0.50, 95% interval 0.33–0.75. However, the authority’s demonstration criterion also requires outcomes among uninstructed passengers, which are absent. Delivery fits £120,000 without clinical supplies. Waiting leaves crowding unchanged; extra vehicles cannot serve every route.\n\n### 4. Necessary conditions\nBefore launch, provide free coverings, accessible instructions and staff briefing. Preserve boarding access, ordinary exemptions without documentation, and other precautions; prohibit physical enforcement. Passengers bear handling, washing and discomfort burdens; staff duties must remain manageable. At three weeks, assess uptake, infections, complaints and access problems; adjust or stop for unacceptable access burdens.\n\n### 5. Decision-changing evidence\nComparable randomised evidence measuring infections among uninstructed passengers, with a two-sided 95% RR interval wholly below 1, would establish the claim. Unacceptable access harms or credible evidence of no meaningful programme benefit would change adoption.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":0.98,"max_output_tokens":8000,"previous_response_id":null,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"status":"completed","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":1199,"input_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":0,"cached_tokens_details":null,"image_to